{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nTokyo’s skyline at dawn was a blur of neon and steel as our bullet train glided into Shinjuku Station. The energy was electrifying—street food stalls hummed, salarymen rushed past, and the scent of miso ramen filled the air. We started with a quick (but delicious) bowl at Ichiran, then wandered through Shinjuku Gyoen, where cherry blossoms dripped pink petals over ancient lanterns.\n\nNext, Osaka’s Dotonbori district exploded in color. Giant crab signs glowed against the night sky, and the sizzle of takoyaki stalls mixed with laughter. We squeezed onto the crowded Sakurayama Observation Deck for a sunset view of the river below, then tried our luck at a karaoke bar—off-key J-pop and sake flowed freely.\n\nKyoto was calmer, a world of temples and tea. We sipped matcha in a serene garden at Kamppi-ji, then got lost in the narrow alleys of Gion, where geisha glimpsed through latticed doors. A late-night stop at Nishiki Market for fresh mochi and pickles felt like stealing a secret.\n\nOur last night was in Hiroshima, where a moment of silence at the Peace Memorial Park gave way to okonomiyaki shared with locals. The Shinkansen hummed us back to Tokyo, leaving us breathless but already dreaming of returning.\n\nJapan in a week? Impossible to capture—just endless layers of wonder.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.30262133479118347}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.04418794438242912}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.012623289600014687}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -5.936446541454643e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -1.174424409866333}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.07322251796722412}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.005896553862839937}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.08479240536689758}, {"token": "Tokyo", "logprob": -1.712857961654663},